       <heapLoc> N:Int => N +Int 1 </heapLoc>
       requires notBool N in_keys(H)
endmodule

codex
I’ve chosen a direct character scanner. It avoids unsupported regular expressions and keeps the proof over arbitrary finite strings: the loop tracks whether it is still before the first word and whether that first word is exactly a pending `I`. Delimiters close/reset a sentence, and modeled whitespace is handled explicitly through the supplied string semantics.
